---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import GatewayLab from '../../components/GatewayLab.astro';
import GatewayIcon from '../../labs/gateway/GatewayIcon.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="The right tools for this task | David Blumenau" description="Try two fictional tasks against recorded evidence from a real local PanelForge gateway run. Inspect tool filtering, policy denial and authenticated user isolation.">
  <main id="main" class="gl-page">
    <section class="gl-hero wrap" id="top"><a class="text-link" href="/work/connected-agents/"><GatewayIcon name="back" /> The connected agents story</a><div class="gl-hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Gateway Lab / A focused permission boundary</p><h1>Give the task<br /><em>room to work.</em></h1></div><div><p>An agent choosing music can search without controlling the room. A host can build a queue while leaving the volume alone.</p><p>I built PanelForge’s gateway to make those boundaries explicit: which tools a resource publishes, what a user may do, and which account the backend receives.</p></div></div><div class="gl-hero-foot"><a href="#gl-title">Choose a task. Try an action. Inspect the boundary.</a><span>Actual gateway execution · fictional services · 14 October 2026</span></div></section>
    <div class="wrap"><GatewayLab /></div>
    <section class="gl-film wrap" aria-label="Recorded gateway exhibit replay"><figure class="video-demo"><div class="video-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Browser recording / replay of executed evidence</p><h3>Four attempts at the boundary</h3></div><video controls preload="none" playsinline poster="/media/gateway/browser-replay.png" aria-label="Recorded browser replay of gateway evidence" aria-describedby="gl-film-caption"><source src="/media/gateway/browser-replay.mp4" type="video/mp4" /><track kind="captions" src="/media/gateway/browser-replay.vtt" srclang="en" label="English" default /></video><figcaption id="gl-film-caption"><strong class="video-provenance">An actual browser recording of this exhibit replaying observed gateway results. Browser pacing is editorial.</strong>The separate gateway run executed the complete archived server with local fictional auth, permission and provider services. The recording shows allowed search, off-list queue denial, allowed queueing and user-policy volume denial.</figcaption><a class="text-link" href="/media/gateway/transcript.txt">Read the captured HTTP/MCP transcript <GatewayIcon name="external" /></a></figure></section>
    <section class="gl-context wrap"><p class="eyebrow">One gateway, several distinct checks</p><h2>A tool list is only<br /><em>the beginning.</em></h2><p>A curated resource helps the model start with useful tools. The gateway also checks the caller’s resource scope and per-user policy before forwarding an allowed tool. For a user-aware resource, the authenticated identity replaces a client-supplied account claim.</p><p>The complete committed gateway entrypoint ran in an isolated local fixture. The interaction above replays its actual results. Native profile behavior is explored separately, including the current fallback to the master catalog.</p><div class="gl-context-links"><a class="text-link" href="/features/gateway-tool-profiles/">The gateway feature story <GatewayIcon name="external" /></a><a class="text-link" href="/features/native-tool-boundary-profiles/">Native profiles and their limits <GatewayIcon name="external" /></a><a class="text-link" href="/media/gateway/transcript.txt">Read every captured request <GatewayIcon name="external" /></a></div></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
